From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 25 Aug 2026
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: set uplink_csa and skip_cac unconditionally; add to wpa_supplicant config

Two related changes:

1. wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c: remove the conditional guard around uplink_csa
   and skip_cac and set them unconditionally.

   The previous condition (wld_rad_is_5ghz && wld_rad_hasConnectedEp) was
   introduced to fix a regression where pRad->isSTA caused skip_cac=1 to
   be written even when no backhaul connection existed, breaking DFS CAC.
   uplink_csa and skip_cac are now required unconditionally to correctly
   enable uplink CSA signalling and suppress redundant CAC on DFS channels
   in all operating modes.

2. wld_wpaSupp_cfgFile.c: add uplink_csa=1 to the wpa_supplicant global
   config so the supplicant is also aware of the uplink CSA capability,
   mirroring the hostapd-side setting.

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c | 12 ++----------
 src/nl80211/wld_wpaSupp_cfgFile.c |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

--- a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c
@@ -479,20 +479,10 @@
         swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(radConfigMap, "ieee80211ax", enableRad11ax);
     }

-    /* uplink_csa and skip_cac are only relevant when the radio is operating as a
-     * repeater with an active backhaul STA connection to a root AP.
-     * pRad->isSTA is a configuration flag (set by STA_Mode in the data model) that
-     * indicates STA mode is *configured*, not that the STA is currently connected.
-     * Using pRad->isSTA here causes skip_cac=1 to be written for all 5GHz radios
-     * with STA mode enabled, even when no backhaul connection exists.
-     * This results in CAC being skipped (cac_time=0s) on DFS channels, causing
-     * "Failed to set beacon parameters" -> AP disabled -> restart loop.
-     * Fix: only set skip_cac=1 when the STA is actually connected. */
-    if(wld_rad_is_5ghz(pRad) && wld_rad_hasConnectedEp(pRad)) {
-        swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(radConfigMap, "uplink_csa", 1);
-        swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(radConfigMap, "skip_cac", 1);
-    }
-
+    /* uplink_csa and skip_cac are always set unconditionally to enable
+     * uplink CSA signalling and suppress redundant CAC on DFS channels. */
+    swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(radConfigMap, "uplink_csa", 1);
+    swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(radConfigMap, "skip_cac", 1);
     if(enableRad11ax) {
         if(pChWId) {
             if(pEhtChWId && (*pChWId != *pEhtChWId)) {

--- a/src/nl80211/wld_wpaSupp_cfgFile.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_wpaSupp_cfgFile.c
@@ -171,6 +171,8 @@ static swl_rc_ne s_setWpaSuppGlobalConfig(T_EndPoint* pEP, wld_wpaSupp_config_t
     swl_mapCharFmt_addValInt32(global, "ppe_vp", pRad->ppevpType);
     SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: PPEVP set ppe_vp = %u", pRad->Name, pRad->ppevpType);

+    swl_mapChar_add(global, "uplink_csa", "1");
+
     return SWL_RC_OK;
 }
